From e1961f48ea835c44b435bdf980451ed37335d19c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <jelon@tbu.net>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 16:42:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 007/206] port(3.12.2): A7/B2/B4 -- vmcode CLI, Shorebird JSON,
 Dart_ShorebirdLoadVmcode

Three upstream features now supersede hand-rolled work, so theirs is used
instead (CLAUDE.md rule 2):

  * A1's globals.h edit forcing the Simulator is obsolete -- upstream added the
    GN arg dart_force_simulator ('Force use of the simulator even when the Dart
    target arch matches the current cpu'), absent at our 3.7 baseline.
  * SIMULATOR_HOST_ARCH_MATCH is dropped for upstream's SIMULATOR_FFI, set by
    runtime/BUILD.gn when dart_force_simulator && arm64. It covers il_arm64.cc,
    stub_code_compiler_arm64.cc and ffi_callback_metadata.cc, which our macro
    never reached, so ffi_dynamic_library.cc reverts to upstream entirely.
  * analyze_snapshot.cc's platform widening is obsolete: upstream dropped the
    android/linux restriction outright.

C3 survives in minimal form -- upstream still conflates 'Simulator compiled in'
with 'codegen targets the Simulator', so SIMULATOR_AVAILABLE is still derived
here, now settable from the command line rather than hard-coded per-arch.

Dropped per rule 1 (Route-A is out of scope): stub_code_compiler.cc's LR-state
fix, which lives inside #if defined(DART_DYNAMIC_MODULES); and the five Gate 1
spike natives with their Dart-side declarations --
runtime/lib/object.cc (121 lines), sdk/lib/internal/internal.dart,
internal_patch.dart, bootstrap_natives.h. 202 lines of retired debt not carried
over.

Conflicts resolved: main_options.h keeps upstream's grown option list and
appends shorebird_vmcode; dart_api_impl.cc keeps both sides.
vm_sources.gni: all 466 registered sources exist. #if/#endif balances.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

